{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpanEventDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"SpanTracer"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SpanTracer"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Tracing6TracerP","text":"Tracer"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The span is found from the record’s "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which was taken when the event was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked, so a delivery that runs later, under another span or none, still adds the event to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right one. Each span event is named after the event, stamped with the time it was tracked,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and carries the event’s description under "},{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and its call site under OpenTelemetry’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"code.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute names."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or whose span has ended by the time it is delivered, has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span to join and is left out: span events can’t be added to a finished span. Batch tightly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enough for spans to outlive their batches, or deliver to another destination as well."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TracingDestinations\/docum